      "question": {
        ":question/id": "f6792163-892d-567c-8d26-c5674dc37aa7",
        ":question/problem": "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n165^\\circ=225^\\circ-60^\\circ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(165^\\circ\\right)$.\n\n$\\cos\\left(165^\\circ\\right)=$ {{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x-y)=\\cos x\\cos y+\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(165^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(225^\\circ-60^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(225^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(60^\\circ\\right)+\\sin\\left(225^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}\\right) \\\\\n&=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
