      "question": {
        ":question/id": "014e904c-4ac0-5d05-ae04-396c1677c3b1",
        ":question/problem": "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n105^\\circ=240^\\circ-135^\\circ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(105^\\circ\\right)$.\n\n$\\cos\\left(105^\\circ\\right)=$ {{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x-y)=\\cos x\\cos y+\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(105^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(240^\\circ-135^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(240^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(135^\\circ\\right)+\\sin\\left(240^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(135^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}+\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{- \\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "2ac3b95d-427a-5a44-a5e3-1e6c55842097",
