        ":question/id": "79666e9c-2f88-5b52-bd7c-67da11dc25a1",
        ":question/problem": "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n-75^\\circ=45^\\circ-120^\\circ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(-75^\\circ\\right)$.\n\n$\\cos\\left(-75^\\circ\\right)=$ {{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x-y)=\\cos x\\cos y+\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(-75^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(45^\\circ-120^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(45^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(120^\\circ\\right)+\\sin\\left(45^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(120^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\\n&=\\frac{- \\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
