        ":question/id": "1445f9a4-ddce-59b1-855c-0727569a68df",
        ":question/problem": "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\frac{23\\pi}{12}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{7\\pi}{4},\n$$\n\ncalculate the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(\\frac{23\\pi}{12}\\right)$.\n\n$\\cos\\left(\\frac{23\\pi}{12}\\right)=$ {{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x+y)=\\cos x\\cos y-\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(\\frac{23\\pi}{12}\\right)=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}-\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
